TI  - Understanding the Wadden Sea as a shared responsibility
AU  - Busch, J.A.
AU  - Bostelmann, A.
AB  - Understanding the Wadden Sea as a shared responsibility. The Wadden Sea is the largest tidal flat system in the world, where natural processes run undisturbed. The World Heritage site is home to over 10,000 species of plants and animals, which continuously adapt to the ever-changing dynamic area. 10–12 million migratory birds yearly rely on the Wadden Sea as a stopover. To ensure its protection, the three countries have been joining efforts for the sea's conservation since 1978, taking responsibility for this irreplaceable ecosystem and preserving it for the benefit of present and future generations. One of the cooperation's main pillars is the harmonised, cross-border Trilateral Monitoring and Assessment Programme. © 2019, Wiley-VCH Verlag. All rights reserved.
