TY  - JOUR
TI  - Proposals for the Baltic monitoring programme (HELCOM BMP) and coastal monitoring programme (HELCOM CMP) for the Polish marine areas of the Baltic Sea
AU  - Andrulewicz, E.
AB  - The present Baltic Monitoring Programme was designed under former political conditions and can be regarded as open-sea oriented monitoring. Recently, however, the political situation has changed fundamentally. The New Helsinki Convention (1992) incorporates territorial and internal waters as well as nature conservation and biodiversity aspects. Proposals for a new Baltic Monitoring Programme should take into account the following constrains and current conditions: the limited national resources available for the monitoring effort; new demands stemming up from the New Helsinki Convention, such as coastal monitoring and monitoring of nature conservation areas; introduction of the new measurement techniques which may soon change the traditional way of studying the sea; and change in monitoring strategy towards the measurement of the biological effects of pollution.
