TI  - Boundary organisations and their strategies: Three cases in the Wadden Sea
AU  - van Enst, WI
AU  - Runhaar, HAC
AU  - Driessen, PPJ
AB  - This article discusses three empirical cases of boundary organisations, within the context of the Wadden Sea: the Wadden Academy, IMSA Amsterdam and the NCEA. The research aims to provide further insights into how boundary organisations work in practice. The research shows that the role of a boundary organisation can be fulfilled by different types of organisations (not solely scientific). Depending on the science-policy interaction problem they face, a boundary organisation can have different goals and use different strategies. Furthermore, the strategic use of media outputs, and the degree of actuality and public debate can have a substantial influence on the practices of boundary organisations. (C) 2015 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
