TI  - Meadow/Pasture Extensification in the Fen Belt of the Elbe Marshlands in Hamburg - Floristic investigations from 1988 to 1998
AU  - Tesch, A.
AB  - The paper presents results from floristic investigations accompanying the protection programme for moist grasslands in Hamburg. From 1988/89 onwards vegetation development was investigated and evaluated on representative contract sites using permanent square plots. On meadows and pastures with moderate species diversity the changed management conditions partly induced significant fluctuations amongst the dominant species. A constant increase of target species (e.g. indicator species for oligotrophic sites, typical species for wetland meadows, endangered species) was only found rarely. Proposals to improve management conditions as well as to optimise aims and implementation of the protection programme are given. They include suggestions to individualise and flexibilise the management conditions with stronger consideration of agricultural usability and to give more priority to conserving remaining moist grasslands.
