AB  - There is now a new dimension beyond fishing and navigation as the sea bottom is developed. It is used as a biological, mineral, and energy source, and as a place to throw fluid and solid wastes. There are more and more ships using the sea and it is used for leisure. Shallow seas are reclaimed. It must be protected. These problems are discussed in relation to the North Sea and its resources, using Jade Bay as an example. -D.J.Davis
